# Local generation and checkpoint directories
outputs/
render/
exports/
artifacts/
checkpoints/

# Reference material that should remain controlled
private/
confidential/
reference-private/

# Do not track generated project metadata files unless explicitly approved
*.bak
*.orig

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DURABLE MEDIA ARTIFACT STORE — deliberate exception to the exclusions above
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The blanket binary patterns above (`*.png`, `*.jpg`, ...) exist to keep
# incidental and scratch media out of the repository. They MUST NOT cover the
# DESIGNATED DURABLE ARTIFACT STORE, which is the fallback store for production
# media when Git LFS is unavailable or unverified (see
# production/media-preservation-policy.md and
# production/media-preservation-register.yaml).
#
#   production/media/**        canonical store for APPROVED ASSET media
#   verification/tests/**      canonical store for test-bench media
#                              (candidates, tested frames, derivatives)
#
# Media in these trees must survive session boundaries and must be recoverable
# by SHA-256 checksum. Never re-cover these paths with a blanket binary
# pattern. Large-format masters that must stay out of ordinary Git tracking go
# to external storage and are recorded in the preservation register with a
# durable URI — they are not simply dropped.
!production/media/**
!verification/tests/**
